NLP + COMPUTER VISION INTERVIEW
200 IMPORTANT HINGLISH Q&A
Basic → Intermediate → Advanced → Production


==================================================
PART A — NLP INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
100 POINTS
==================================================


==============================
LEVEL 1 — NLP FUNDAMENTALS
==============================


1. QUESTION:
NLP kya hai?

ANSWER:
NLP yani Natural Language Processing AI ka ek domain hai jisme machines ko human language ko understand, process, analyze aur generate karne ki capability di jaati hai.

Examples:
- Chatbots
- Sentiment Analysis
- Translation
- Text Classification
- Search
- Summarization
- Question Answering


2. QUESTION:
NLP ka real-world use kahan hota hai?

ANSWER:
NLP ka use:

- Chatbots
- Voice assistants
- Spam detection
- Search engines
- Recommendation systems
- Sentiment analysis
- Document processing
- Machine translation
- Customer support

mein hota hai.


3. QUESTION:
NLP aur Generative AI mein kya relation hai?

ANSWER:
NLP broader field hai jo human language processing ko cover karta hai.

Generative AI language ko generate bhi kar sakta hai.

LLMs NLP ke advanced applications mein se ek hain.


4. QUESTION:
Text Classification kya hai?

ANSWER:
Text ko predefined categories/classes mein assign karna text classification hai.

Example:

Email → Spam

Customer message → Complaint

Review → Positive/Negative


5. QUESTION:
Sentiment Analysis kya hai?

ANSWER:
Text mein expressed sentiment ya emotion identify karna sentiment analysis hai.

Example:

"I love this product."

Output:
Positive.


6. QUESTION:
Named Entity Recognition kya hai?

ANSWER:
NER text mein important entities identify karta hai.

Examples:

"Rahul works at Microsoft in Delhi."

Entities:

Rahul → PERSON
Microsoft → ORGANIZATION
Delhi → LOCATION


7. QUESTION:
Text Summarization kya hai?

ANSWER:
Large text/document ko shorter meaningful summary mein convert karna text summarization hai.


8. QUESTION:
Machine Translation kya hai?

ANSWER:
Ek language ke text ko doosri language mein translate karna machine translation hai.

Example:

English → Hindi

Hindi → Arabic


9. QUESTION:
Question Answering kya hai?

ANSWER:
User ke question ko understand karke relevant answer generate ya retrieve karna Question Answering system ka purpose hai.


10. QUESTION:
Information Extraction kya hai?

ANSWER:
Unstructured text se structured information extract karna Information Extraction hai.

Example:

"Order 12345 was delivered on Monday."

Extract:

Order ID = 12345
Date = Monday


11. QUESTION:
Tokenization kya hai?

ANSWER:
Text ko smaller units called tokens mein divide karna tokenization hai.

Example:

"I love AI"

Tokens:

I
love
AI


12. QUESTION:
Word Tokenization kya hai?

ANSWER:
Text ko words ke basis par split karna word tokenization hai.


13. QUESTION:
Character Tokenization kya hai?

ANSWER:
Text ko individual characters mein divide karna character tokenization hai.

Example:

AI

A
I


14. QUESTION:
Subword Tokenization kya hai?

ANSWER:
Words ko smaller meaningful subword units mein break karna subword tokenization hai.

Modern LLMs mein subword tokenization widely use hoti hai.


15. QUESTION:
BPE kya hai?

ANSWER:
BPE yani Byte Pair Encoding frequent character/subword combinations ko merge karke vocabulary build karta hai.

Isse unknown words ko bhi smaller subwords mein represent karna possible hota hai.


16. QUESTION:
WordPiece kya hai?

ANSWER:
WordPiece subword tokenization technique hai jo vocabulary ko efficiently represent karti hai.

BERT family mein WordPiece commonly associated hai.


17. QUESTION:
SentencePiece kya hai?

ANSWER:
SentencePiece raw text ko language-independent way mein tokenize kar sakta hai aur whitespace par dependent nahi hota.


18. QUESTION:
Stop Words kya hote hain?

ANSWER:
Common words jaise:

the
is
a
an
of

ko traditional NLP pipelines mein stop words kaha jata hai.

Lekin modern transformer applications mein blindly stop-word removal karna zaroori nahi hota.


19. QUESTION:
Stemming kya hai?

ANSWER:
Word ko simplified root-like form mein reduce karna stemming hai.

Example:

playing
played
plays

→ play


20. QUESTION:
Lemmatization kya hai?

ANSWER:
Word ko linguistically valid base form yani lemma mein convert karna lemmatization hai.

Example:

better → good

Lemmatization generally stemming se more linguistically meaningful hoti hai.


==============================
LEVEL 2 — TEXT REPRESENTATION
==============================


21. QUESTION:
Bag of Words kya hai?

ANSWER:
Bag of Words text ko word occurrence/frequency ke numerical representation mein convert karta hai.

Isme word order generally preserve nahi hota.


22. QUESTION:
TF-IDF kya hai?

ANSWER:
TF-IDF yani Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency kisi document mein word ki importance measure karta hai.

Common words ka weight reduce aur relatively distinctive words ka weight increase ho sakta hai.


23. QUESTION:
TF kya hai?

ANSWER:
Term Frequency batata hai ki kisi document mein ek particular term kitni frequently appear hoti hai.


24. QUESTION:
IDF kya hai?

ANSWER:
Inverse Document Frequency measure karta hai ki term poore document collection mein kitni rare hai.

Jo word har document mein common hai uska IDF low hota hai.


25. QUESTION:
Word Embedding kya hai?

ANSWER:
Word ya text ko dense numerical vector mein represent karna embedding hai.

Embedding semantic relationships capture karne ki koshish karta hai.


26. QUESTION:
Word2Vec kya hai?

ANSWER:
Word2Vec neural-network-based technique hai jo words ko vector space mein represent karti hai.

Similar context wale words ke embeddings often nearby hote hain.


27. QUESTION:
CBOW kya hai?

ANSWER:
CBOW yani Continuous Bag of Words surrounding/context words se target word predict karta hai.


28. QUESTION:
Skip-Gram kya hai?

ANSWER:
Skip-Gram target word ko use karke surrounding context words predict karta hai.


29. QUESTION:
GloVe kya hai?

ANSWER:
GloVe yani Global Vectors word embeddings learn karta hai using global word co-occurrence statistics.


30. QUESTION:
Static aur Contextual Embeddings mein difference?

ANSWER:
Static embedding mein ek word ka generally fixed vector hota hai.

Contextual embedding mein same word ka representation surrounding context ke according change ho sakta hai.


31. QUESTION:
Contextual Embedding kya hai?

ANSWER:
Word ka representation uske sentence context ke according generate hona contextual embedding hai.

Example:

"I went to the bank."

"The river bank was beautiful."

Dono cases mein "bank" ka meaning different hai.


32. QUESTION:
Cosine Similarity kya hai?

ANSWER:
Do vectors ke beech semantic/angular similarity measure karne ke liye cosine similarity commonly use hoti hai.


33. QUESTION:
Dense Vector kya hai?

ANSWER:
Dense vector mein most dimensions meaningful numerical values contain karti hain.

Embeddings generally dense vectors hote hain.


34. QUESTION:
Sparse Vector kya hai?

ANSWER:
Sparse vector mein large number of dimensions zero ho sakti hain.

Bag-of-Words aur TF-IDF representations commonly sparse ho sakte hain.


35. QUESTION:
Semantic Similarity kya hai?

ANSWER:
Do text inputs meaning ke level par kitne similar hain, semantic similarity measure karta hai.


==============================
LEVEL 3 — NLP PREPROCESSING
==============================


36. QUESTION:
Text Cleaning kya hai?

ANSWER:
Raw text se unwanted noise remove ya normalize karna text cleaning hai.

Examples:

- Extra spaces
- Unwanted HTML
- Invalid characters
- Duplicate content
- Encoding issues


37. QUESTION:
Lowercasing kyun karte hain?

ANSWER:
Traditional NLP mein uppercase/lowercase variations ko normalize karne ke liye lowercasing use hoti thi.

Lekin transformer-based NLP mein case information useful ho sakti hai, isliye blindly lowercase nahi karna chahiye.


38. QUESTION:
Regular Expression ka NLP mein use?

ANSWER:
Regex ka use:

- Pattern extraction
- Email extraction
- Phone extraction
- Data cleaning
- Rule-based preprocessing

ke liye hota hai.


39. QUESTION:
N-gram kya hai?

ANSWER:
N-gram consecutive N tokens ka sequence hota hai.

Example:

"machine learning"

Bigram = machine learning


40. QUESTION:
Unigram, Bigram aur Trigram kya hain?

ANSWER:

Unigram = 1 word

Bigram = 2 consecutive words

Trigram = 3 consecutive words


41. QUESTION:
Text Normalization kya hai?

ANSWER:
Different text representations ko consistent format mein convert karna text normalization hai.


42. QUESTION:
Handling spelling errors kaise karenge?

ANSWER:
Approach:

- Dictionary lookup
- Edit distance
- Spell correction models
- Transformer-based correction

use kar sakte hain.


43. QUESTION:
Edit Distance kya hai?

ANSWER:
Ek string ko doosri string mein convert karne ke liye required minimum insert, delete aur substitute operations ki count edit distance hoti hai.


44. QUESTION:
Language Detection kya hai?

ANSWER:
Given text kis language mein hai, identify karna language detection hai.

Multilingual AI systems mein useful hai.


45. QUESTION:
Multilingual NLP kya hai?

ANSWER:
Multiple human languages ko process karne wale NLP systems multilingual NLP systems hote hain.


==============================
LEVEL 4 — MACHINE LEARNING NLP
==============================


46. QUESTION:
NLP mein classification models kaunse use kar sakte hain?

ANSWER:

- Logistic Regression
- Naive Bayes
- SVM
- Decision Trees
- Random Forest
- Neural Networks
- Transformers


47. QUESTION:
Naive Bayes NLP mein kyun popular tha?

ANSWER:
Naive Bayes simple, fast aur text classification ke liye effective baseline model hai.

Spam classification mein historically widely used hua hai.


48. QUESTION:
SVM NLP mein kaise use hota hai?

ANSWER:
Text ko numerical feature representation mein convert karke SVM classification boundary learn karta hai.

TF-IDF + SVM traditional NLP ka strong baseline ho sakta hai.


49. QUESTION:
NLP mein class imbalance kaise handle karenge?

ANSWER:

- Class weights
- Resampling
- Threshold tuning
- F1 score
- Precision/Recall
- Better dataset collection

use kar sakte hain.


50. QUESTION:
NLP model ko kaise evaluate karenge?

ANSWER:
Task ke according metrics choose karenge.

Classification:
- Accuracy
- Precision
- Recall
- F1

Generation:
- BLEU
- ROUGE
- BERTScore
- Human Evaluation
- LLM-based evaluation


==============================
LEVEL 5 — SEQUENCE MODELS
==============================


51. QUESTION:
RNN kya hai?

ANSWER:
RNN yani Recurrent Neural Network sequential data ko process karne ke liye design kiya gaya neural network architecture hai.

Previous hidden state ko next step mein use kiya jata hai.


52. QUESTION:
RNN ki limitation kya hai?

ANSWER:
Long sequences mein vanishing/exploding gradients ke wajah se long-term dependencies learn karna difficult ho sakta hai.


53. QUESTION:
LSTM kya hai?

ANSWER:
LSTM yani Long Short-Term Memory RNN ka improved architecture hai jo gates ke through long-term information ko maintain karne ki capability improve karta hai.


54. QUESTION:
LSTM mein gates kaunse hote hain?

ANSWER:

- Forget Gate
- Input Gate
- Output Gate

Ye information ko control karne mein help karte hain.


55. QUESTION:
GRU kya hai?

ANSWER:
GRU yani Gated Recurrent Unit LSTM ka comparatively simpler gated architecture hai.

Isme fewer gates hote hain aur architecture simpler hota hai.


56. QUESTION:
RNN vs LSTM?

ANSWER:
RNN simple hai lekin long-term dependencies mein struggle kar sakta hai.

LSTM gating mechanism ke through long-term dependencies ko better handle karta hai.


57. QUESTION:
Sequence-to-Sequence model kya hai?

ANSWER:
Ek input sequence ko doosre output sequence mein transform karne wala architecture sequence-to-sequence model hai.

Machine translation iska classic example hai.


58. QUESTION:
Encoder kya karta hai?

ANSWER:
Encoder input sequence ko useful internal representation mein encode karta hai.


59. QUESTION:
Decoder kya karta hai?

ANSWER:
Decoder encoded representation ke basis par output sequence generate karta hai.


60. QUESTION:
Attention mechanism ki need kyun hui?

ANSWER:
Long sequence mein entire information ko ek fixed representation mein compress karna difficult tha.

Attention model ko relevant input parts par dynamically focus karne deta hai.


==============================
LEVEL 6 — TRANSFORMERS
==============================


61. QUESTION:
Transformer kya hai?

ANSWER:
Transformer sequence processing architecture hai jo self-attention mechanism ka use karta hai aur modern NLP/LLMs ka major foundation hai.


62. QUESTION:
Transformer ka main advantage kya hai?

ANSWER:
Transformer parallel processing enable karta hai aur long-range token relationships ko effectively model kar sakta hai.


63. QUESTION:
Self-Attention kya hai?

ANSWER:
Self-attention input sequence ke tokens ke beech relationships calculate karta hai aur har token ke liye relevant contextual information aggregate karta hai.


64. QUESTION:
Query, Key aur Value kya hain?

ANSWER:
Query batata hai current token kis information ko search kar raha hai.

Key batata hai har token kis type ki information provide karta hai.

Value actual information represent karta hai jo output mein contribute karti hai.


65. QUESTION:
Attention Score kya hai?

ANSWER:
Query aur Key ke relationship se attention score calculate hota hai.

High score ka matlab generally stronger relevance indicate karta hai.


66. QUESTION:
Multi-Head Attention kya hai?

ANSWER:
Multiple attention heads different representation subspaces mein relationships learn karte hain.

Isse model multiple types ke dependencies capture kar sakta hai.


67. QUESTION:
Positional Encoding kya hai?

ANSWER:
Transformer ko token order ki information dene ke liye positional information add ki jaati hai.


68. QUESTION:
Encoder-only Transformer kya hai?

ANSWER:
Encoder-only models input understanding/representation tasks ke liye commonly useful hote hain.

Example:
BERT.


69. QUESTION:
Decoder-only Transformer kya hai?

ANSWER:
Decoder-only architecture autoregressive text generation ke liye commonly use hoti hai.

Modern generative LLMs ka major architecture pattern hai.


70. QUESTION:
Encoder-Decoder Transformer kya hai?

ANSWER:
Encoder input ko represent karta hai aur decoder output generate karta hai.

Machine translation aur sequence-to-sequence tasks mein useful hai.


==============================
LEVEL 7 — ADVANCED NLP / LLM
==============================


71. QUESTION:
BERT kya hai?

ANSWER:
BERT yani Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers transformer-based language representation model hai.

Ye contextual text understanding ke tasks ke liye widely influential raha hai.


72. QUESTION:
GPT kya hai?

ANSWER:
GPT family decoder-style autoregressive language models par based hai jo next-token prediction ke through language generation learn karte hain.


73. QUESTION:
Masked Language Modeling kya hai?

ANSWER:
Sentence ke kuch tokens hide/mask karke model se missing tokens predict karwana Masked Language Modeling hai.

BERT-style training mein iska use hota hai.


74. QUESTION:
Next Token Prediction kya hai?

ANSWER:
Previous tokens ke context ke basis par next token predict karna autoregressive language modeling ka core objective hai.


75. QUESTION:
Pretraining kya hai?

ANSWER:
Large-scale general dataset par model ko broad language patterns learn karwana pretraining hai.


76. QUESTION:
Fine-Tuning kya hai?

ANSWER:
Pretrained model ko specific task ya domain dataset par further train karke behavior adapt karna fine-tuning hai.


77. QUESTION:
Instruction Tuning kya hai?

ANSWER:
Model ko instructions aur corresponding desired responses ke examples par train karke instruction-following capability improve karna instruction tuning hai.


78. QUESTION:
RLHF kya hai?

ANSWER:
RLHF yani Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback mein human preferences ka use karke model behavior ko align karne ki koshish ki jaati hai.


79. QUESTION:
Hallucination kya hai?

ANSWER:
Jab language model confident-sounding but incorrect ya unsupported information generate karta hai, usse hallucination kehte hain.


80. QUESTION:
NLP mein hallucination kaise reduce karenge?

ANSWER:

- RAG
- Grounded prompts
- Tool usage
- Retrieval validation
- Structured output
- Human evaluation
- Model evaluation
- Confidence/verification mechanisms

use kar sakte hain.


==============================
LEVEL 8 — NLP PRODUCTION
==============================


81. QUESTION:
NLP application ko production mein kaise deploy karenge?

ANSWER:

User
→ API
→ Preprocessing
→ Model
→ Postprocessing
→ Response

Production mein additionally:

- Authentication
- Logging
- Monitoring
- Rate limiting
- Error handling
- Scaling

add karenge.


82. QUESTION:
NLP model latency kaise reduce karenge?

ANSWER:

- Smaller model
- Quantization
- Batching
- Caching
- Efficient tokenization
- Model optimization
- GPU inference
- Async processing

use kar sakte hain.


83. QUESTION:
NLP model caching kya hai?

ANSWER:
Frequently repeated ya semantically similar requests ke results cache karke unnecessary model inference reduce kar sakte hain.


84. QUESTION:
Batch inference NLP mein kab useful hai?

ANSWER:
Jab real-time response ki requirement nahi ho aur large amount of documents process karne ho.

Example:
Daily 1 million documents classify karna.


85. QUESTION:
Streaming response kya hai?

ANSWER:
Complete response ka wait karne ke instead generated output ko incremental chunks/tokens mein client ko send karna streaming response hai.


86. QUESTION:
NLP pipeline monitoring mein kya track karenge?

ANSWER:

- Latency
- Error rate
- Token usage
- Model quality
- Input distribution
- Output quality
- Drift
- Cost


87. QUESTION:
NLP Model Drift kya hai?

ANSWER:
Production input data ya language patterns time ke saath change hone se model performance degrade ho sakti hai.

Isse data/concept drift ke context mein monitor kiya ja sakta hai.


88. QUESTION:
Prompt Versioning kya hai?

ANSWER:
Production prompts ko version control ke through maintain karna prompt versioning hai.

Isse prompt changes ka impact track kar sakte hain.


89. QUESTION:
NLP application mein security risks kya hain?

ANSWER:

- Prompt injection
- Data leakage
- PII exposure
- Malicious input
- Unauthorized API access
- Prompt extraction
- Excessive tool permissions


90. QUESTION:
NLP system ka cost optimize kaise karenge?

ANSWER:

- Smaller models
- Token reduction
- Prompt optimization
- Caching
- Batching
- Model routing
- Quantization
- Efficient retrieval

use karenge.


==============================
LEVEL 9 — ADVANCED NLP SYSTEM DESIGN
==============================


91. QUESTION:
Enterprise NLP Search System ka architecture?

ANSWER:

Documents
→ Cleaning
→ Chunking
→ Embeddings
→ Vector DB

User Query
→ Query Embedding
→ Hybrid Search
→ Reranking
→ Results


92. QUESTION:
Enterprise RAG NLP system ka architecture?

ANSWER:

Document Ingestion
→ Parsing
→ Chunking
→ Embedding
→ Vector Database

User
→ Query
→ Retrieval
→ Reranking
→ Context
→ LLM
→ Validation
→ Response


93. QUESTION:
NLP system mein Hybrid Search kyun use karenge?

ANSWER:
Keyword search exact terms ko capture karta hai.

Vector search semantic meaning capture karta hai.

Dono ko combine karne se retrieval quality improve ho sakti hai.


94. QUESTION:
NLP mein Reranker kyun use karenge?

ANSWER:
Initial retrieval broad candidates return kar sakta hai.

Reranker un candidates ko deeper relevance ke basis par reorder karta hai.


95. QUESTION:
NLP system mein metadata filtering ka benefit?

ANSWER:
Search ko specific attributes ke according restrict kar sakte hain.

Example:

Department = Finance

Year = 2026

Document Type = Policy


96. QUESTION:
NLP system ko multilingual kaise banayenge?

ANSWER:

- Multilingual embeddings
- Language detection
- Multilingual LLM
- Translation layer
- Language-specific evaluation

use kar sakte hain.


97. QUESTION:
NLP system ke liye model kaise choose karenge?

ANSWER:
Factors:

- Accuracy
- Language support
- Context window
- Latency
- Cost
- Deployment options
- Privacy
- Hardware requirement
- Fine-tuning support


98. QUESTION:
NLP interview mein project kaise explain karenge?

ANSWER:

Problem
→ Data
→ Preprocessing
→ Model
→ Training
→ Evaluation
→ API
→ Deployment
→ Monitoring
→ Business Impact


99. QUESTION:
Senior NLP Engineer ke liye important skills kya hain?

ANSWER:

- Python
- NLP
- Transformers
- LLMs
- Embeddings
- RAG
- Vector DB
- APIs
- MLOps
- Evaluation
- Security
- System Design


100. QUESTION:
NLP Engineer ka production-level answer kaise dena chahiye?

ANSWER:
Answer mein sirf model ka naam nahi bolna chahiye.

Explain:

Problem
→ Why this approach
→ Data
→ Model
→ Evaluation
→ API
→ Deployment
→ Latency
→ Cost
→ Monitoring
→ Security
→ Business Impact



==================================================
PART B — COMPUTER VISION INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
100 POINTS
==================================================


==============================
LEVEL 1 — COMPUTER VISION FUNDAMENTALS
==============================


101. QUESTION:
Computer Vision kya hai?

ANSWER:
Computer Vision AI ka domain hai jisme machines images aur videos ko understand, analyze aur interpret karna seekhti hain.


102. QUESTION:
Computer Vision ke real-world applications?

ANSWER:

- Face Detection
- Face Recognition
- OCR
- Object Detection
- Autonomous Vehicles
- Medical Imaging
- Surveillance
- Quality Inspection
- Image Search
- Document Processing


103. QUESTION:
Image kya hoti hai?

ANSWER:
Digital image pixels ka collection hoti hai.

Har pixel intensity ya color information represent karta hai.


104. QUESTION:
Pixel kya hai?

ANSWER:
Pixel digital image ka smallest individual picture element hai.

Image ka visual information pixels ke through represent hota hai.


105. QUESTION:
Image Resolution kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image mein total horizontal aur vertical pixels ki dimensions resolution define karti hain.

Example:

1920 × 1080


106. QUESTION:
Grayscale Image kya hai?

ANSWER:
Grayscale image mein generally har pixel ek intensity value represent karta hai.

Usually black se white tak intensity range hoti hai.


107. QUESTION:
RGB Image kya hai?

ANSWER:
RGB image mein har pixel ke liye:

Red
Green
Blue

channels hote hain.


108. QUESTION:
RGB aur Grayscale mein difference?

ANSWER:
RGB image mein three color channels hote hain.

Grayscale image mein generally one intensity channel hota hai.

Grayscale computationally simpler ho sakti hai.


109. QUESTION:
Image Channel kya hai?

ANSWER:
Channel image ke ek information dimension ko represent karta hai.

RGB image mein three channels hote hain:

R
G
B


110. QUESTION:
Pixel Intensity kya hai?

ANSWER:
Pixel intensity pixel ke brightness/value ko represent karti hai.

Grayscale images mein common 8-bit representation mein values 0 se 255 tak hoti hain.


==============================
LEVEL 2 — IMAGE PROCESSING
==============================


111. QUESTION:
Image Preprocessing kya hai?

ANSWER:
Model ko input dene se pehle image ko clean, resize, normalize ya transform karna image preprocessing hai.


112. QUESTION:
Image Resizing kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image ke dimensions ko required size mein convert karna resizing hai.

Deep learning models fixed ya controlled input dimensions expect kar sakte hain.


113. QUESTION:
Image Normalization kya hai?

ANSWER:
Pixel values ko suitable numerical range mein scale karna normalization hai.

Example:

0–255
→
0–1


114. QUESTION:
Image Cropping kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image ke selected region ko extract karna cropping hai.


115. QUESTION:
Image Padding kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image ke borders par additional pixels add karna padding hai.

Aspect ratio preserve karne ya fixed dimensions achieve karne ke liye use ho sakta hai.


116. QUESTION:
Data Augmentation kya hai?

ANSWER:
Training images ke modified versions create karke dataset diversity increase karna data augmentation hai.


117. QUESTION:
Common Image Augmentation techniques?

ANSWER:

- Rotation
- Flipping
- Cropping
- Scaling
- Translation
- Brightness change
- Contrast change
- Noise
- Color jitter


118. QUESTION:
Data Augmentation kyun use karte hain?

ANSWER:
Dataset diversity increase karne aur overfitting reduce karne ke liye data augmentation useful hai.


119. QUESTION:
Image Filtering kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image ko smooth, sharpen ya specific patterns emphasize karne ke liye filters apply karna image filtering hai.


120. QUESTION:
Gaussian Blur kya hai?

ANSWER:
Gaussian blur image ko smooth karta hai aur high-frequency noise/details ko reduce kar sakta hai.


==============================
LEVEL 3 — IMAGE PROCESSING ADVANCED
==============================


121. QUESTION:
Convolution kya hai?

ANSWER:
Convolution operation mein kernel/filter image par slide karta hai aur local pixel patterns ko detect karta hai.


122. QUESTION:
Kernel kya hai?

ANSWER:
Kernel ek small matrix/filter hota hai jo image ke local region par operation perform karta hai.

Different kernels different patterns detect kar sakte hain.


123. QUESTION:
Edge Detection kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image mein sharp intensity changes identify karna edge detection hai.

Edges objects ki boundaries identify karne mein useful hain.


124. QUESTION:
Sobel Operator kya hai?

ANSWER:
Sobel operator image mein horizontal aur vertical intensity gradients detect karne ke liye use hota hai.


125. QUESTION:
Canny Edge Detection kya hai?

ANSWER:
Canny ek multi-stage edge detection algorithm hai jo noise reduction, gradient detection aur edge selection ke through edges identify karta hai.


126. QUESTION:
Thresholding kya hai?

ANSWER:
Pixel intensity ke basis par image ko regions/classes mein divide karna thresholding hai.


127. QUESTION:
Binary Image kya hai?

ANSWER:
Binary image mein pixels generally do possible values/classes represent karte hain.

Example:

0
and
1


128. QUESTION:
Morphological Operations kya hain?

ANSWER:
Binary ya grayscale image structures ko modify/process karne ke operations morphological operations kehlate hain.

Common operations:

- Erosion
- Dilation
- Opening
- Closing


129. QUESTION:
Erosion kya hai?

ANSWER:
Erosion foreground regions ko shrink kar sakta hai aur small noise/remove structures ko eliminate karne mein useful ho sakta hai.


130. QUESTION:
Dilation kya hai?

ANSWER:
Dilation foreground regions ko expand kar sakta hai aur small gaps ko connect karne mein useful ho sakta hai.


==============================
LEVEL 4 — CNN
==============================


131. QUESTION:
CNN kya hai?

ANSWER:
CNN yani Convolutional Neural Network image data se spatial patterns learn karne ke liye specialized neural network architecture hai.


132. QUESTION:
CNN mein Convolution Layer kya karti hai?

ANSWER:
Convolution layer image se local features learn karti hai.

Early layers:
- Edges
- Corners
- Textures

Later layers:
- Shapes
- Object parts
- High-level features

learn kar sakti hain.


133. QUESTION:
Pooling kya hai?

ANSWER:
Pooling feature maps ka spatial size reduce karta hai aur important information ko retain karne ki koshish karta hai.


134. QUESTION:
Max Pooling kya hai?

ANSWER:
Local region mein maximum activation select karna max pooling hai.

Ye strong detected feature ko preserve kar sakta hai.


135. QUESTION:
Average Pooling kya hai?

ANSWER:
Local region ke activations ka average calculate karna average pooling hai.


136. QUESTION:
CNN mein ReLU kyun use hota hai?

ANSWER:
ReLU non-linearity introduce karta hai aur convolutional networks mein efficient activation function ke roop mein widely used hai.


137. QUESTION:
CNN mein Stride kya hai?

ANSWER:
Filter image par kitne pixels ka step lekar move karega, usse stride kehte hain.


138. QUESTION:
Padding kya hai CNN mein?

ANSWER:
Input ke borders par additional values/pixels add karna padding hai.

Padding output size control aur border information preserve karne mein help kar sakti hai.


139. QUESTION:
Same aur Valid Padding?

ANSWER:
Same padding generally output spatial dimensions ko input ke similar maintain karne ke liye use hoti hai.

Valid padding mein additional padding nahi hoti aur output dimensions reduce ho sakti hain.


140. QUESTION:
Receptive Field kya hai?

ANSWER:
Network ka koi neuron input image ke kitne spatial region ko indirectly observe kar raha hai, us region ko receptive field kehte hain.


==============================
LEVEL 5 — IMAGE CLASSIFICATION
==============================


141. QUESTION:
Image Classification kya hai?

ANSWER:
Complete image ko predefined class/category assign karna image classification hai.

Example:

Cat
Dog
Car


142. QUESTION:
Binary Image Classification kya hai?

ANSWER:
Jab model ko two classes mein se ek choose karni ho.

Example:

Defective
vs
Non-Defective


143. QUESTION:
Multi-Class Classification kya hai?

ANSWER:
Multiple classes mein se exactly one class predict karna multi-class classification hai.


144. QUESTION:
Multi-Label Classification kya hai?

ANSWER:
Ek image mein simultaneously multiple labels assign karna multi-label classification hai.

Example:

Image:
Dog + Car + Person


145. QUESTION:
Transfer Learning kya hai?

ANSWER:
Pretrained model ke learned visual features ko new task/dataset mein reuse karna transfer learning hai.


146. QUESTION:
Transfer Learning Computer Vision mein kyun useful hai?

ANSWER:
Large image dataset se pretrained features reuse karne ke karan limited domain data mein training faster aur often more effective ho sakti hai.


147. QUESTION:
Image classification model kaise evaluate karenge?

ANSWER:

- Accuracy
- Precision
- Recall
- F1
- Confusion Matrix
- Per-class metrics


148. QUESTION:
Confusion Matrix Computer Vision mein kya batati hai?

ANSWER:
Classification model ne kaunsi classes correctly ya incorrectly predict ki hain, confusion matrix se identify kar sakte hain.


149. QUESTION:
Class Imbalance Computer Vision mein kaise handle karenge?

ANSWER:

- Class weights
- Oversampling
- Augmentation
- Balanced dataset
- Focal Loss
- Appropriate metrics


150. QUESTION:
Focal Loss kya hai?

ANSWER:
Focal Loss difficult/misclassified examples par relatively more focus karta hai.

Object detection aur class imbalance problems mein useful ho sakta hai.


==============================
LEVEL 6 — OBJECT DETECTION
==============================


151. QUESTION:
Object Detection kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image mein objects ko identify karna aur unki locations bounding boxes ke through detect karna object detection hai.


152. QUESTION:
Object Detection aur Classification mein difference?

ANSWER:
Classification batata hai image mein kya hai.

Object detection batata hai:

Kya hai?
+
Kahan hai?


153. QUESTION:
Bounding Box kya hai?

ANSWER:
Object ke around rectangular coordinates define karna bounding box hai.


154. QUESTION:
IoU kya hai?

ANSWER:
IoU yani Intersection over Union predicted bounding box aur ground-truth bounding box ke overlap ko measure karta hai.

Formula:

IoU =
Intersection Area
/
Union Area


155. QUESTION:
IoU ka use kahan hota hai?

ANSWER:
IoU ka use:

- Detection evaluation
- Positive/negative matching
- NMS
- Localization quality

mein hota hai.


156. QUESTION:
YOLO kya hai?

ANSWER:
YOLO yani You Only Look Once real-time object detection family hai jo detection ko efficient single-stage approach ke through perform karti hai.


157. QUESTION:
Two-Stage Detector kya hai?

ANSWER:
Two-stage detector pehle candidate regions propose karta hai aur phir un regions ko classify/localize karta hai.

Faster R-CNN iska famous example hai.


158. QUESTION:
One-Stage Detector kya hai?

ANSWER:
One-stage detector directly image se object classes aur locations predict karta hai.

YOLO family aur SSD common examples hain.


159. QUESTION:
NMS kya hai?

ANSWER:
NMS yani Non-Maximum Suppression overlapping bounding boxes mein se strongest prediction retain karke duplicate detections suppress karta hai.


160. QUESTION:
Object Detection mein Precision aur Recall kyun important hain?

ANSWER:
Detection mein false positives aur false negatives dono important hote hain.

Precision false detections ko measure karne mein useful hai.

Recall missed objects ko measure karne mein useful hai.


==============================
LEVEL 7 — SEGMENTATION
==============================


161. QUESTION:
Image Segmentation kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image ko meaningful regions/pixels mein divide karna image segmentation hai.


162. QUESTION:
Semantic Segmentation kya hai?

ANSWER:
Har pixel ko class assign karna semantic segmentation hai.

Same class ke multiple objects ko generally same category treat kiya jata hai.


163. QUESTION:
Instance Segmentation kya hai?

ANSWER:
Har individual object instance ko separately segment karna instance segmentation hai.

Example:

Person 1
Person 2
Person 3


164. QUESTION:
Semantic vs Instance Segmentation?

ANSWER:
Semantic segmentation:
Pixel → Class

Instance segmentation:
Pixel → Individual Object Instance


165. QUESTION:
Mask kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image ke pixels par selected region/object ko represent karne wali binary ya probability map ko mask kaha ja sakta hai.


166. QUESTION:
U-Net kya hai?

ANSWER:
U-Net encoder-decoder style architecture hai jo especially biomedical image segmentation mein highly influential raha hai.


167. QUESTION:
Encoder ka segmentation mein role?

ANSWER:
Encoder image se progressively high-level features extract karta hai aur spatial dimensions reduce kar sakta hai.


168. QUESTION:
Decoder ka role?

ANSWER:
Decoder feature representation se spatial resolution restore karke pixel-level prediction generate karta hai.


169. QUESTION:
Skip Connection kya hai?

ANSWER:
Earlier layers ki spatial/detail information ko later layers ke saath connect karna skip connection hai.

Segmentation architectures mein fine-grained details recover karne mein useful hai.


170. QUESTION:
Segmentation ko kaise evaluate karenge?

ANSWER:

- IoU
- Dice Score
- Pixel Accuracy
- Precision
- Recall

use kar sakte hain.


==============================
LEVEL 8 — OCR + DOCUMENT VISION
==============================


171. QUESTION:
OCR kya hai?

ANSWER:
OCR yani Optical Character Recognition image/document mein present text ko machine-readable text mein convert karta hai.


172. QUESTION:
OCR pipeline kya ho sakti hai?

ANSWER:

Document/Image
→ Preprocessing
→ Text Detection
→ Text Recognition
→ Postprocessing
→ Structured Output


173. QUESTION:
OCR preprocessing mein kya karenge?

ANSWER:

- Resize
- Denoising
- Deskew
- Contrast enhancement
- Thresholding
- Cropping


174. QUESTION:
Document AI kya hai?

ANSWER:
Documents ko visually understand karke text, tables, fields aur semantic information extract karna Document AI hai.


175. QUESTION:
Invoice processing kaise automate karenge?

ANSWER:

Invoice
→ OCR
→ Field Detection
→ Entity Extraction
→ Validation
→ Structured JSON
→ Database/API


176. QUESTION:
Handwritten Text Recognition kya hai?

ANSWER:
Handwritten text ko image se identify karke digital text mein convert karna Handwritten Text Recognition hai.


177. QUESTION:
Table Extraction kya hai?

ANSWER:
Document image/PDF mein tables identify karke rows, columns aur cell values ko structured format mein convert karna table extraction hai.


178. QUESTION:
Document Layout Analysis kya hai?

ANSWER:
Document ke visual regions jaise:

- Heading
- Paragraph
- Table
- Image
- Footer
- Header

identify karna layout analysis hai.


179. QUESTION:
OCR accuracy kaise improve karenge?

ANSWER:

- Better image quality
- Deskewing
- Denoising
- Proper cropping
- Better OCR model
- Language-specific model
- Post-processing
- Confidence filtering


180. QUESTION:
OCR errors kaise handle karenge?

ANSWER:
OCR output ko validation rules, dictionaries, regex, confidence scores aur downstream language models ke through verify/correct kar sakte hain.


==============================
LEVEL 9 — ADVANCED COMPUTER VISION
==============================


181. QUESTION:
Vision Transformer kya hai?

ANSWER:
Vision Transformer yani ViT image ko patches mein divide karke transformer architecture ke through image relationships learn karta hai.


182. QUESTION:
CNN vs Vision Transformer?

ANSWER:
CNN strong local inductive biases aur convolution operations use karta hai.

Vision Transformer image patches ko token-like representation mein convert karke self-attention use karta hai.

Dono architectures ke trade-offs dataset, scale, compute aur task par depend karte hain.


183. QUESTION:
Image Patch kya hai?

ANSWER:
Vision Transformer mein image ko small fixed-size regions/patches mein divide kiya jata hai.

Har patch ko embedding/token representation mein convert kiya ja sakta hai.


184. QUESTION:
Multimodal AI kya hai?

ANSWER:
Text, image, audio ya video jaise multiple modalities ko ek AI system mein process/combine karna multimodal AI hai.


185. QUESTION:
Vision-Language Model kya hai?

ANSWER:
Vision-Language Model image aur text dono ko process karke cross-modal understanding ya generation perform kar sakta hai.


186. QUESTION:
Image Captioning kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image ko analyze karke natural-language description generate karna image captioning hai.


187. QUESTION:
Visual Question Answering kya hai?

ANSWER:
Image aur natural-language question dono ko input dekar image-based answer generate karna VQA hai.


188. QUESTION:
Object Tracking kya hai?

ANSWER:
Video ke multiple frames mein same object ki identity aur location ko continuously track karna object tracking hai.


189. QUESTION:
Detection aur Tracking mein difference?

ANSWER:
Object detection har frame mein objects locate karta hai.

Tracking detected objects ko frames ke across same identity ke saath follow karta hai.


190. QUESTION:
Video Analytics kya hai?

ANSWER:
Video streams ko process karke events, objects, activities aur behaviors identify karna video analytics hai.


==============================
LEVEL 10 — PRODUCTION COMPUTER VISION
==============================


191. QUESTION:
Computer Vision model ko production mein kaise deploy karenge?

ANSWER:

Image/Video
→ API/Stream
→ Preprocessing
→ Model Inference
→ Postprocessing
→ Business Logic
→ Response

Production mein monitoring, security aur scaling bhi add karenge.


192. QUESTION:
Computer Vision inference latency kaise reduce karenge?

ANSWER:

- Model quantization
- Smaller architecture
- Image resizing
- Batch inference
- GPU acceleration
- TensorRT/optimized runtime
- Model pruning
- Efficient preprocessing


193. QUESTION:
Model Quantization kya hai?

ANSWER:
Model weights/activations ko lower numerical precision mein represent karna quantization hai.

Isse model size aur inference cost/latency reduce ho sakti hai, although accuracy impact evaluate karna zaroori hai.


194. QUESTION:
Computer Vision model mein Data Drift kya hai?

ANSWER:
Production images ka distribution training data se significantly change ho jaye to model performance degrade ho sakti hai.

Example:

Training:
Daytime images

Production:
Night-time CCTV images


195. QUESTION:
Computer Vision model monitoring mein kya track karenge?

ANSWER:

- Inference latency
- Error rate
- Confidence scores
- Class distribution
- Image quality
- Data drift
- Detection metrics
- GPU utilization
- Throughput


196. QUESTION:
Low-quality images ko kaise handle karenge?

ANSWER:

- Image quality checks
- Blur detection
- Resolution checks
- Brightness checks
- Preprocessing
- Image enhancement
- Reject/flag low-quality inputs


197. QUESTION:
Computer Vision system ko scalable kaise banayenge?

ANSWER:

- Containerization
- GPU inference servers
- Horizontal scaling
- Load balancing
- Batch processing
- Queue-based architecture
- Model optimization
- Async processing


198. QUESTION:
Real-time CCTV Computer Vision architecture explain karein.

ANSWER:

CCTV Camera
→ Video Stream
→ Frame Sampling
→ Preprocessing
→ Object Detection
→ Tracking
→ Event Detection
→ Alert Service
→ Database
→ Dashboard

Production mein GPU inference, monitoring aur alert deduplication bhi add karenge.


199. QUESTION:
Senior Computer Vision Engineer se kya expect hota hai?

ANSWER:
Senior CV Engineer ko sirf model train karna nahi, balki:

- Problem formulation
- Data strategy
- Model selection
- Evaluation
- Optimization
- Deployment
- GPU utilization
- Monitoring
- Scalability
- Security
- Business impact

explain karna aana chahiye.


200. QUESTION:
Computer Vision project ko interview mein kaise explain karenge?

ANSWER:

Business Problem
→ Dataset
→ Data Cleaning
→ Annotation
→ Augmentation
→ Model Selection
→ Training
→ Evaluation
→ Error Analysis
→ Optimization
→ API/Deployment
→ Monitoring
→ Business Impact


